timestamp=2026-11-05T12:54:57.038Z level=INFO run=e7dc0897 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# The column that matches calib (\"power_reading \" with space) has value 80.0 - let us look at FARM_D's capacity or typical values? Also calibration offset for FARM_D is 80.0. Calibration offset is (recorded value) - (true value). So true value = recorded value - offset. If recorded is 80.0 and offset is 80.0, true value becomes 0.0. That also makes sense for night time? And the other column gives 0.0 already. That’s suspicious.\n# Also look at another time of day - during daytime maybe?\npath = '/app/dataset/production_FARM_D.csv'\nwith open(path, 'rb') as f:\n    b = f.read(2)\nenc = 'utf-16le' if b == b'\\xff\\xfe' else 'utf-8'\ndf = pd.read_csv(path, encoding=enc, sep=',', skiprows=3)\n# find a daytime row\nfor i in range(10, 20):\n    print(i, df.iloc[i]['timestamp\\t'], df.iloc[i]['power_reading '], df.iloc[i]['power_reading'])\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
