timestamp=2026-11-05T12:56:06.641Z level=INFO run=e7dc0897 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Also need to parse timestamps correctly. Timestamps are in local time of the farm? Or UTC? Let us look at the task: \"Compute the total real energy production in kilowatt-hours (kWh) on the UTC reporting day 2024-03-15 (the half-open window [2024-03-15 00:00:00 UTC, 2024-03-16 00:00:00 UTC))\"\n# So we must filter readings whose timestamps, when interpreted correctly, fall within that UTC window. The timestamps in the CSVs - are they in UTC or in farm local time? That’s critical. The maintenance windows are \"provided in the farm's local civil time\" - that suggests production timestamps might also be in local time? Or UTC? Let us look at examples. For instance, FARM_C is Sakura Energy Site in Asia/Tokyo (UTC+9). Maintenance notes mention system firmware update on Sakura Energy Site (FARM_C) on 16th March from 08:00 to 12:00 local time - and also panel inspection on 15th March 09:00-11:00 local time (cancelled). We need to exclude readings during successfully conducted maintenance windows. So to compare, we need to convert maintenance window times (local) to UTC or convert production timestamps to UTC.\n# So production timestamps - what timezone are they in? The files might be in local time. Or maybe UTC. Let us look at FARM_C (Tokyo) data around those times. Firmware update on 16th March 08:00-12:00 local Tokyo time (UTC+9). That means UTC is 16th March 23:00 (previous day) to 17th March 03:00? 08:00 JST is 23:00 UTC previous day. 12:00 JST is 03:00 UTC same day? Wait 08:00 JST (UTC+9) is UTC-9? No: JST is UTC+9, so 08:00 JST = 23:00 UTC on 15th March (08:00 - 9h = 23:00 previous day). 12:00 JST = 03:00 UTC on 16th March. The maintenance is on 16th March 08:00-12:00 local time - so in UTC that’s 15th 23:00 to 16th 03:00 UTC. Also the reporting day is 2024-03-15 UTC (window 00:00:00 UTC 15th to 00:00:00 UTC 16th). So this maintenance window (15th 23:00 UTC to 16th 03:00 UTC) spans across the boundary of 15th UTC - part of it is on 15th UTC (from 23:00 onwards) and part on 16th UTC. If status is COMPLETED, readings during that window must be excluded. That means on reporting day 2024-03-15 UTC, readings from 23:00 UTC onward on 15th UTC (if in UTC) would be excluded? That depends on whether production timestamps are in UTC. Let us look at FARM_C’s actual timestamps.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
